<title>USA: St. Jude acquisition clears hurdle.</title>
<headline>St. Jude acquisition clears hurdle.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>St. Jude Medical Inc said Wednesday the Hart-Scott-Rodino antitrust review period for its planned acquisition of Telectronics Pacing Systems Inc from Pacific Dunlop Ltd had expired.</p>
<p>The acquisition of Telectronics is expected to close before the end of the fourth quarter, the company said.</p>
<p>In October, St. Jude Medical said it agreed to pay a total of $135 million for Englewood, Colorado-based Telectronics and Medtel, an Asia-Pacific medical products distribution business.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
